purpose operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "Append one printable key to the edit buffer when there is room."
invariant operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "The target buffer remains null-terminated and currentLength never grows past capacity minus one."
warning appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "Only single-byte printable ASCII input (codepoints 32..126) is accepted. Multi-byte UTF-8 input, terminal paste blocks, control characters, and IME composition sequences are silently dropped here; supporting them requires a UTF-8 decoder and a separate paste-mode reader, neither of which exists yet."
label startAppendPrintableKeyToBuffer
storage local immutable oneStep Int64 1
# rationale: The inclusive ASCII printable range. 32 = ' ' (space, the lowest
# printable character) and 126 = '~' (tilde, the highest before DEL at 127).
# Bytes outside [32..126] are dropped — see the warning on this operation.
storage local immutable minPrintableKey Int32 32
storage local immutable maxPrintableKey Int32 126
call belowPrintableCheckCall math.lessThanInt32
argument belowPrintableCheckCall left Int32 keyCode
argument belowPrintableCheckCall right Int32 minPrintableKey
