purpose operation renderScreen "Render the todo TUI from heap-backed arrays with a fixed-width edit modal."
invariant operation renderScreen "The visible row loop emits at most visibleRows rows and does not mutate todo state."
invariant operation renderScreen "editBuffer is an opaque memory pointer that callers guarantee holds a null-terminated byte sequence: writeEmptyBuffer seeds the first byte with NUL on allocation, and appendPrintableKeyToBuffer / deleteLastBufferByte maintain the terminator at every length change. renderScreen passes editBuffer to c.printf as a %s argument, which relies on that invariant."
warning renderScreen "modalValueFormatText's `%-47.47s` edit-modal title column silently truncates titles longer than 47 bytes on screen. The full editBuffer (up to titleCapacity-1 = 127 bytes) is still in memory; only the modal view is clipped. The character-count line below (modalMetaFormatText) shows the true length so an editor of a long title knows the visible region is partial."
